The invention concerns a process for generating and/or collecting neutrons, comprising the following operations:  

a) subjecting nuclei chosen from protons, deuterons and/or tritons to an electric field, so that the nuclei are extracted and guided toward a target (20) that contains free electrons;  

b) optionally applying a spatial and/or time-varying gradient of a first magnetic field to the nuclei, in order to impose a predetermined orientation on their magnetic moments;  

c) alternatively, applying a second magnetic field to the target so as to align the magnetic moments of the target’s free electrons in a predetermined manner;  

d) or employing an electron-donating superparamagnetic material, such that the electrons in the free layers of that material become oriented along preferred directions produced by the orientation of the material’s resultant magnetic moment;  

e) optionally, when a superparamagnetic material is used, avoiding exposure of the proton beam and/or the target to external magnetic fields.  

A heating apparatus and/or a magnetic-field-generating apparatus may be necessary to activate the material’s superparamagnetic characteristics.
